.TH SINDOOK-DOCTOR 1 "2026-08-18" "sindook 0.7.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
sindook-doctor \- diagnose the sindook installation
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sindook doctor
[\fB\-json\fP] [\fB\-check-version\fP]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Checks the health of the local installation: the running binary, the
portable configuration directory and its contents, and platform
properties the commands rely on. Prints findings and remediation
advice. Useful as a first step after installation or before filing a
bug report.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-json\fP
machine-readable output, one JSON object
.TP
\fB\-check-version\fP
also compare the running version against the latest GitHub release
and report when an update is available
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
no problems found
.TP
.B 1
one or more problems found, or the check could not complete
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sindook (1),
.BR sindook-paths (1),
.BR sindook-selftest (1)
